mira-cs: FYI BrightCart web is back in our queue. Their QA reported a huge spike of preflight 429s during onboarding from the single-page web app. Seen around 15:20 UTC.

devin-cs: Any hint whether this is mobile SDK or browser?

mira-cs: Browser. They said multiple tabs + service worker background sync. Browser logs show many parallel preflight requests from different contexts.

ash-eng: That explains it — service worker + multiple tabs can each trigger the ephemeral exchange. If they're using the SDK in-page + the SW, you'll get cross-context fanout.

ash-eng: Short triage: can you grab the console dump and any SW network slices?

mira-cs: Pasted a snippet from their console: 
```
[service-worker] fetch /v1/preflight -> started
main-tab: fetch /v1/preflight -> started
other-tab: fetch /v1/preflight -> started
response: 429 x-retry-after: 20
```

kai-sre: We should confirm whether tokens are stored in both localStorage and the SW scope. If they're not coordinating, each context will exchange separately.

devin-cs: They said they used localStorage for tokens and SW reads directly from fetch events so it doesn't see the tab-local cache.

ash-eng: Mitigation recommendations: 1) Move token storage to IndexedDB (accessible from both SW and main threads) + use a tiny locking protocol to avoid thundering herd. 2) Use BroadcastChannel to notify other tabs of a recently fetched token. 3) Add a short de-dup window in the SDK (coalesce preflights within 500ms). 4) ServiceWorker should prefer cached session token and only trigger exchange if token absent/expired.

ash-eng: Example IndexedDB retrieval + lock (pseudo):
```js
// in main + SW
const token = await idb.get('session_token');
if(!token){
  if(await tryLock('exch_lock')){
    const newTok = await fetch('/exchange');
    idb.set('session_token', newTok, 60);
    releaseLock('exch_lock');
    broadcast.postMessage({token:newTok});
  } else {
    // wait for broadcaster to provide token
    await waitForBroadcastToken(1000);
  }
}
```

mira-cs: From CS side: the customer is on a trial org and worried about hitting renewal risks if onboarding is slow. They asked for a short term uplift while they patch.

kai-sre: I can open a temporary preflight grace window for their org (brightcart-web-09) for 90 minutes and lower the strictness threshold for the SW agent. Need confirmation.

devin-cs: Confirmed org_id=brightcart-web-09, region=us-west-2. Please also expose a metric for preflight origin (user-agent+sw) so we can filter in dashboards.

ratebot: :white_check_mark: Policy change applied by kai-sre  per-org preflight window enabled for brightcart-web-09, TTL 90m. ChangeRef: policy-2026-09-12-0283

mira-cs: Customer applied the IndexedDB + BroadcastChannel patch to their staging sample app and saw concurrent preflights drop to 0 within minutes. They will roll to production tomorrow morning.

devin-cs: Can we add a short onboarding note: "Browser apps using service workers should use shared token storage (IndexedDB) or server-side session tokens; avoid per-context exchange". Also add a sample BroadcastChannel snippet to the docs.

ash-eng: Will add a recommended code sample to the web SDK README and a migration note for SW users. I'll also add a de-dup toggle in the SDK (enabled by default).

mira-cs: Thanks team. I'll add a line to the onboarding checklist to ask whether the customer uses service workers/multi-tab flows and offer to request temporary burst windows. Closing this thread after follow-up doc PR. :handshake:
